From c8f75ab0694a3bfce7349e4dd7dd6c6d7d231f52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: armSeb <armSeb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:30:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add LG G3 LGD SIC 1440p dual DSI video panel

Panel driver for the 1440x2560 LGD "SIC" video mode panel of the LG G3
(D855), driven over two DSI links (720x2560 each, 4 lanes). Init and off
sequences and timings come from the vendor device tree
(msm8974pro-lge-panel.dtsi), power sequencing from the vendor driver
(mdss_dsi.c, mdss_dsi_panel.c). Supplies: vdd (1.8 V), vsp/vsn (TPS65132,
+/-5.0 V).

Like the vendor driver:
- the panel the bootloader left running is taken over as it is
  (continuous splash), without reset nor init sequence;
- the off sequence is sent from .disable, while the video stream still
  runs (once the MDP interface has stopped, the DSI video engine no
  longer leaves room for commands);
- VSP/VSN are cut and reset asserted while the screen is off;
- the init sequence starts with a DCS soft reset: the reset line alone
  does not bring the panel back.

Signed-off-by: armSeb <armSeb@users.noreply.github.com>
